WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.534
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody!

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.367
Everyone's in a good mood.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.567
Everyone's in a good mood.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.767
You guys, tomorrow is
Thanksgiving!

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:10.901
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:15.133
Right now, some of you are
excited to see your family,

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.767
while the rest of you
are about to draw

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.267
an extra line on a COVID test.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.334
You're like, "Aw!"

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:22.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:24.734
A bit of history --
I read that Abraham Lincoln

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:29.033
declared Thanksgiving an
official holiday in 1863.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.767
It's like during the Civil War,

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:32.601
he saw our country fighting
each other and thought,

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.100
"We should make a whole meal
out of this."

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.834
That's right, Thanksgiving is
almost here and nobody is more

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.634
in the spirit
than local news anchors.

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:41.968
Let's see how they're
celebrating.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:43.834
-Gobble, gobble, gobble.
-Gobble, gobble, gobble.

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:45.200
-Gobble, gobble.
-Gobble, gobble.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.801
-Gobble, gobble.
-Gobble, gobble, gobble.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:50.968
[ Gobbling ]

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:55.167
-Gobble, gobble, gobble, gobble.
Huh, huh?

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.501
-Did you purposely wear
turkey colors today?

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.200
You kind of look like
a big ol' butterball.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.033
-Thanks. Thanks a lot, Abby.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:04.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:06.968
-Wow!
-Then during the commercial,

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.033
she tried pulling Abby's arm off
like a wishbone.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:12.033
It's like, "Hey, what do you
mean?" Look like a butterball.

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:15.267
Tomorrow is Thanksgiving, but
tonight is Drinks-giving.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:20.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.200
Why am I telling you guys?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.734
I feel like you know this
already.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.133
Drinks-giving, that's when a lot
of people hit up

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.234
their hometown bars
to see old friends.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.634
It's a great tradition.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:30.667
You talk smack about your family
to your friends,

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.167
and then tomorrow you talk smack

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.400
about your friends
to your family.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.767
[ Laughter ]
It's a good time.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.067
It's basically an entire bar
filled with people saying,

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:39.701
"Tim's looking like
a big ol' butterball."

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.000
This is actually one of the
biggest drinking nights

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.901
of the year, which is why
tomorrow morning people are

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.367
going to be like,
"I'm most thankful for

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.067
this bacon, egg, and cheese
and Gatorade."

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:51.267
[ Laughter and applause ]
Love it.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:52.534
Tonight, a lot of people went to

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:54.267
their hometown bar
with old friends.

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:55.901
But if you weren't able to go
out, don't worry.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:57.400
We put together a simulation of

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.667
how your conversation
would have gone.

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.133
Take a look at this.

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:23.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:26.801
-Get it, get it, bro.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:30.434
Let's get at it, bro.

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:31.901
Get it, bro.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:33.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.067
Guys, I'm so pumped
it's Thanksgiving Eve.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:37.334
Just think, in 12 hours, your
aunt's going to pull a turkey

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:39.200
out of the oven
that isn't plant-based

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.601
but it's definitely beyond meat.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:42.334
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:45.133
Meanwhile, speaking of food,
Ocean Spray says they flip

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:47.968
the labels on their cranberry
sauce cans upside-down

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:52.300
to create a "seamless serving
experience."

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.100
You know, when you're dumping
a brick of maroon slime

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.367
out of a can, you're really
playing fast and loose

00:02:58.367 --> 00:03:00.100
with the phrase
"serving experience."

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:02.434
Seriously, I don't even like

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:04.968
the sound it makes
when it comes out.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.267
Eww.
-[ Slurp sound ]

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:07.501
-Yeah. Don't --

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:11.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.834
That's right,
people all over the country

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:13.901
are getting ready for tomorrow.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:15.300
Quest, you all prepped
for Thanksgiving?

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.601
-Yeah, man. I got everything
I need at the grocery store.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.501
I just landed on a sweet potato

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:20.701
casserole recipe
I'm going to make.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.300
And, you know, that's it.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.901
How about you?
-I'm ready too.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.000
We're having family over.
So I rented some tables.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.968
I got my Thanksgiving playlist
ready to go.

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.334
What are you going to do,
Higgins?

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.234
-Oh, man, I'm so ready
for Thanksgiving.

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:32.801
Before I left the house
this morning,

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.801
I cranked up the oven
at 600 degrees.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.400
-Higgins, you're not supposed to
leave your oven on

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.567
when you're not home.
-Oh, relax, it's fine.

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:41.968
My oven takes a little while
to heat up

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.400
because the gas line has a hole
in it.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:46.234
It stinks up the kitchen so bad.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:48.567
I left a bunch of aerosol cans
right next to the oven.

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.634
And when I get home,
I'm going to spray them down

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:52.367
and freshen up the place.
-No, no, Higgins, you --

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.000
-I know, I know, you're probably
worried that the turkey

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.634
won't get fully cooked because
of the busted gas line.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.067
We got a backup bird.

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:01.834
Wrapped it in foil.
Popped it in the microwave.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.901
Set it for nine hours.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.167
And get this.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:06.767
We're going to deep-fry
that sucker.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.667
[ Laughter ]
Got a great deal.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:11.667
Found 18 leaky propane tanks
on the side of the highway.

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:14.200
Man, it is going to be
a good Thanksgiving!

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.200
Hoo!

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.834
[ Ding ]
-Oh.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.167
Oh, no.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:22.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.934
My neighbor's house blew up.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:27.167
I knew I should have been
cooking at my house.

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:28.767
So no, I'm not ready.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.701
-Oh, my God.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.167
Your neighbor's house?

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:35.033
Hey, this is fun.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.000
Tomorrow is the Macy's
Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:43.334
The Roots and I will be there
performing.

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:46.300
But if you love parades, Macy's
isn't the only game in town.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.400
Watch this.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.133
-Tired of parades
with trendy balloons

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:50.968
that people actually
want to see?

00:04:50.968 --> 00:04:54.367
Then tune in to the T.J. Maxx
Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:56.934
The only parade with
old, out of fashion balloons

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:59.067
that Macy's threw away
years ago.

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.734
Like Ask Jeeves,

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:02.567
the Pets.com dog,

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:04.634
weird old guy Superman,

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:06.701
and whatever the hell this is.

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:10.100
T.J. Maxx, where every day looks
like the day after Black Friday!

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:14.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.033
-Well, with Thanksgiving Day
so close,

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:18.167
I think it's time to read
that classic story

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:21.400
we all know and love.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:25.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:29.200
♪♪

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.601
'Twas the night
before Thanksgiving,

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:33.400
and, oh, what a night.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.033
Not a creature was sober,
chugging Miller High Life.

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:37.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:40.167
The dive bars were packed,
everyone playing pool

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.834
in the hopes they'd hook up with
someone from high school.

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:44.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.901
When all of a sudden,
there arose such a titter.

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:50.367
Oh, no, Elon Musk posted another
weird meme to Twitter.

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:53.367
I rolled both my eyes and turned
off my phone,

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:56.634
then went to my parents' house
to watch "Yellowstone."

00:05:56.634 --> 00:06:00.601
On John Dutton, on Beth Dutton,
on Teeter and Kayce,

00:06:00.601 --> 00:06:02.701
on Rip Wheeler,
on Chief Rainwater,

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.267
everyone except Jamie.

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:06.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:10.634
Then I sprang to my childhood
bedroom to crash,

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:13.734
but my cousin was in there
smoking his stash.

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:16.467
Tomorrow, I thought,
my whole family will fight.

00:06:16.467 --> 00:06:18.400
But happy Thanksgiving to all,

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.601
except my Uncle Steve,
who I hope misses his flight.

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:29.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.067 --> 00:06:32.234
Well, this is going viral.

00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:34.567
A photo that President Biden
posted on Twitter.

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:35.501
Did you see this, Quest?

00:06:35.501 --> 00:06:37.234
-Nah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:40.501
You're going laugh.
It has an optical illusion

00:06:40.501 --> 00:06:44.234
that makes his jacket
look like his legs.

00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:45.601
Look at this photo.

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:53.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.133
People walked into the office
like, "Whoa, I'll come back."

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:57.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.801 --> 00:06:59.100
Can we see that again?

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.801
He looks like a teacher
who would say,

00:07:02.801 --> 00:07:04.767
"You don't have to call me
Mr. Duncan. Call me Matt."

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:06.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:07.767
"You know what?
Forget today's lesson.

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:09.000
Let's just talk about life."

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.434
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.434 --> 00:07:12.501
Yeah, it's the best Biden
optical illusion since

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:14.868
he and Jill looked like
giants next to the Carters.

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:18.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:18.801 --> 00:07:20.067
Remember that? Remember that?

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:22.267
[ Applause ]

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:24.067
-That was the best.
-That was insane.

00:07:26.334 --> 00:07:27.901
Did you guys see this?
Last night ahead of

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:29.300
the Senate runoff in Georgia,

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.801
Herschel Walker was on Fox News,
and he had a bit of a slipup

00:07:32.801 --> 00:07:34.467
while talking about
the election.

00:07:34.467 --> 00:07:35.467
Listen to this.

00:07:40.033 --> 00:07:42.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:42.834 --> 00:07:44.167
-Oh!

00:07:44.167 --> 00:07:47.501
[ Applause ]

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:49.534
-Somebody's excited about
the runoffs.

00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:51.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.367
Switching gears, Elon Musk
reportedly told

00:07:53.367 --> 00:07:55.968
Twitter employees that he's done
laying people off

00:07:55.968 --> 00:07:58.501
and is now
looking to start hiring.

00:07:58.501 --> 00:08:01.000
Elon knew he needed more people
when he looked around

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.834
the Twitter office and saw fewer
than 280 characters.

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:05.601
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:08.067
Hey, this Saturday is
Small Business Saturday,

00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:10.300
and I heard that to attract
younger customers,

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.634
small business owners
are being encouraged

00:08:12.634 --> 00:08:15.000
to up their TikTok game.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.434
Yeah, that's got to be tough,
huh?

00:08:16.434 --> 00:08:18.267
After 50 years of owning
a hardware store,

00:08:18.267 --> 00:08:19.834
mom and pop gotta
stay in business

00:08:19.834 --> 00:08:21.667
by slapping each other
with tortillas.

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:25.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:25.501 --> 00:08:27.367
"We were
the Greatest Generation."

00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:29.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.868 --> 00:08:32.534
What are we doing?

00:08:32.534 --> 00:08:34.567
And finally, a mall in Canada

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:37.200
has an attraction called
Woody the Christmas Tree.

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.868 --> 00:08:41.968
And he just woke up.
Check this out.

00:08:41.968 --> 00:08:45.234
-One, two, three!

00:08:45.234 --> 00:08:48.667
[ Cheering ]

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:58.534
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.534 --> 00:09:01.634
-And that's the first promo for
"A Very Squid Game Christmas."

00:09:01.634 --> 00:09:03.167
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.167 --> 00:09:04.701
Coincidentally, "Wake Up Woody"

00:09:04.701 --> 00:09:06.968
is also Herschel Walker's
new campaign slogan.

00:09:06.968 --> 00:09:08.634
We have a great show tonight.

